# Staging-first cloud delivery

When work goes **beyond the current API/contract baseline** (durable Postgres, Auth0, real payments, staging/prod behavior, or mobile proving the cloud stack), read **`docs/sdlc/staging-first-cloud-delivery.md`** first.

Phases (same names as in that doc):

- **Postgres & event log** — staging Postgres, migrations, event-log path per ADR 0003.
- **Auth & payments (staging)** — Auth0, payments on staging per ADR 0004.
- **Clients prove staging** — mobile + web E2E against **staging** (not production).
- **Projection & sync hardening** — live projection, sync health, contract-backed reads; do not reintroduce in-memory as source of truth after **Postgres & event log** is authoritative.

Optional GitHub labels when tagging issues: **`postgres-event-log`**, **`auth-payments-staging`**, **`staging-client-e2e`**, **`projection-sync-hardening`**. Staging-first: no new cloud-only behavior in production before staging soak.
